Subject: Add HealthCheck.List to the vendored dskit grpcutil package

Origin: DHI-internal (compatibility shim for the grpc-go bump on Loki 2.9)
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/grafana/loki.git ffcd570f815ccf0588bda305659d0d4e925e4ef1
Verify: cmd `go build -o /dev/null ./cmd/loki && echo built` expect "built"
Forwarded: not-needed (Loki 2.9 is end-of-life upstream and takes no further changes)
Drop-When: never: Loki 2.9 is end-of-life upstream and keeps its 2023 dskit snapshot in vendor/

The grpc-go releases that the package build raises Loki 2.9 to declare a List method on the grpc_health_v1 HealthServer interface. The dskit snapshot vendored by Loki 2.9.17 implements only Check and Watch on HealthCheck, so cmd/loki no longer compiles against the bumped grpc. This file adds List to HealthCheck and answers Unimplemented, like the Watch method beside it.

--- /dev/null
+++ b/vendor/github.com/grafana/dskit/grpcutil/health_check_list.go
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+package grpcutil
+import (
+  "context"
+  "github.com/gogo/status"
+  "google.golang.org/grpc/codes"
+  "google.golang.org/grpc/health/grpc_health_v1"
+)
+func (h *HealthCheck) List(_ context.Context, _ *grpc_health_v1.HealthListRequest) (*grpc_health_v1.HealthListResponse, error) {
+  return nil, status.Error(codes.Unimplemented, "Listing is not supported")
+}
